---
// Catalogue entry. Dutch mirror: ./nl/index.astro (edit both together).
import CataloguePage from "../../components/hall/CataloguePage.astro";
const img = "/images/brief-aan-jan/prototype-20-09-2026";
---
<CataloguePage
  lang="en"
  path="/jan-truijen/"
  portrait
  title="Brief aan Jan Truijen | The Lions Alliance"
  description="A talking portrait for museums. Visitors type a letter on an antique typewriter, and the portrait, a screen in a period frame, answers in character with an AI voice and 3D facial animation."
  crumb="Talking portrait"
  h1="Brief aan Jan Truijen"
  facts={[
    ["Object", "Talking portrait installation"],
    ["Visitors use", "Only an antique typewriter"],
    ["The portrait", "A screen in a period frame, with AI voice and 3D facial animation"],
    ["Status", "Working prototype"],
    ["Shown", "Museum Medelo, Meijel, 20 September 2026"],
  ]}
  lede="Visitors type a letter to Jan Truijen on an antique typewriter. He reads it and answers aloud, in character, from the museum&rsquo;s own archive."
  plate={{
    src: `${img}/IMG20260920135209.webp`, w: 1600, h: 2134, vt: "exhibit-jan",
    alt: "The portrait of Jan Truijen in a wooden period frame: a screen showing the painting, with a letter on the desk in front of him",
    caption: "The portrait in its frame at Museum Medelo. The painting is a screen; his face moves as he speaks. Prototype setup: the keyboard was for testing only.",
  }}
  cta={{ href: "/contact/", label: "Enquire about a portrait" }}
  link={{ href: "#venue", label: "How it adapts to your venue" }}
>
  <section class="cat-section">
    <h2>A letter to the past, answered</h2>
    <p>Jan Truijen (1838&ndash;1919) was Meijel&rsquo;s mayor, surveyor, town clerk and MP, and his portrait hangs in Museum Medelo. Visitors sit down at an antique typewriter, the only thing they touch, and type him a letter. When the letter is sent, Jan reads it and replies aloud, in character, with an AI voice and real-time 3D facial animation.</p>
    <p>His answers come from the historical archive, and he says so when he doesn&rsquo;t know something.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="cat-section">
    <h2>From typed letter to spoken reply</h2>
    <ol class="cat-steps">
      <li><div><strong>The visitor types a letter</strong><span>On the typewriter at the desk. Nothing else to learn or press.</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>The letter is matched against the archive</strong><span>Everything the museum&rsquo;s archive holds about him.</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>A reply is composed</strong><span>Grounded in what is actually known about him.</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Jan answers aloud</strong><span>In an AI voice, in character.</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>The portrait moves with him</strong><span>His face animates on the screen in sync with the words.</span></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="cat-section">
    <h2>Where it stands</h2>
    <p>We showed it to the public for the first time at Museum Medelo&rsquo;s members-only opening on 20 September 2026. It was a working prototype, not yet a permanent unattended installation, and a keyboard still sat beside the typewriter for testing. The finished installation uses only the typewriter.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="cat-section" id="venue">
    <h2>The same setup, with your own portrait</h2>
    <p>Medelo is the first venue. The format is built to travel: a different historical figure, a different place, the same setup.</p>
    <div class="cat-lists">
      <div>
        <h3>What stays the same</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The setup and the visitor&rsquo;s path, from typed letter to spoken reply.</li>
          <li>The hardware on site.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>What we make for your venue</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The historical figure who answers.</li>
          <li>The archive the figure draws on.</li>
          <li>The input. It doesn&rsquo;t have to be a typewriter.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="plates">
    <figure class="cat-plate cat-plate--wide">
      <img src={`${img}/IMG20260920135157.webp`} width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="The installation at Museum Medelo: an antique desk with the typewriter and the framed portrait, Jan Truijen's costume beside it and a stained-glass window behind" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 2.</b> The desk at Museum Medelo, with Jan&rsquo;s costume beside it. Prototype setup: the keyboard was there for testing only.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="cat-plate">
      <img src={`${img}/IMG20260920135204.webp`} width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="Close view of the desk: the typewriter on the right, the portrait on a small easel, a clipboard and pen on the left" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 3.</b> The typewriter and the portrait on the desk, seen from the visitor&rsquo;s chair.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="enquiry">
    <div class="cat-enquiry__grid">
      <div>
        <h2>Bring a talking portrait to your venue</h2>
        <p>If your museum, heritage site or historic house has a portrait and an archive, write to us. We reply within one or two working days.</p>
        <div class="cat-enquiry__actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="tla-btn">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-enquiry__for">
        Made for
        <ul>
          <li>Regional and local-history museums</li>
          <li>Heritage societies and archives</li>
          <li>Historic houses and estates</li>
          <li>Tourism organisations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</CataloguePage>
